{"content":"Fixed. `api_error_message` now picks the label as `err["status"] || err["code"] || "ERROR"` (the suggested snippet), and also handles OAuth-style bodies where `error` is a string with `error_description` — so a token failure renders `invalid_grant: bad jwt` instead of raw JSON. Every other/empty/unparseable shape keeps the trimmed raw-body fallback.

Pinned by a new table test in `flutter_app/fastlane/test/play_listing_sync_test.rb` (`gh-1261 rework: api_error_message falls back to code/ERROR/OAuth labels`): code-only body → `400: …`, message-only body → `ERROR: …` (no leading `: ` — the pre-fix behavior was reproduced red first), OAuth body → `invalid_grant: …`, the recorded incident payload still renders `INVALID_ARGUMENT: …`, non-JSON still falls back raw.
","path":"/home/runner/work/flutter_agent_harness/flutter_agent_harness/outputs/review_replies/thread_1.md"}

{"content":"Fixed. `bearer!`, `begin_edit!`, `list_locales!`, and `commit_edit!` now route their failure bodies through `api_error_message`, so the whole module fails readably — e.g. `edits.insert failed (HTTP 400): 400: Package not found` instead of a raw JSON blob. A grep confirms no `res[:body][0, 300]` dump remains anywhere in `flutter_app/fastlane/*.rb`.

Pinned by a new test block (`gh-1261 rework: bearer!/begin_edit!/list_locales!/commit_edit! fail readably`) with injectable error responses added to `FakePlayHttp` (`token_response`, `edit_insert_error`, `listings_error`, `commit_error`): each wrapper raises its `LABEL: message` rendering with no `{` in the message.
","path":"/home/runner/work/flutter_agent_harness/flutter_agent_harness/outputs/review_replies/thread_2.md"}

{"content":"Fixed. `MANAGED_TYPES` now carries the requested comment stating it is the module-local guard (not the full `AppImageType` enum) and must be extended in lock-step with `clear_plan`/`expected_state`/`sync_and_verify!` when adding managed types. The `validate_image_type!` rejection message also names the constant (`managed here (MANAGED_TYPES)`), so the coupling is visible at runtime, not just in the comment.

Pinned by a new test (`gh-1261 rework: validate_image_type! pins MANAGED_TYPES (extend-on-add)`): every managed type passes; a real-but-unmanaged enum value (`tvScreenshots`) is rejected pre-flight with a message naming the value and `MANAGED_TYPES`.
","path":"/home/runner/work/flutter_agent_harness/flutter_agent_harness/outputs/review_replies/thread_3.md"}

